# Auto push & publish

The owner tests on the live site (`r.bhd-om.com`), not locally.

After finishing a coherent change set that is ready to verify on production:

1. Update `CHANGELOG.md` when the change is user-facing.
2. Commit with a clear message (no need to ask first).
3. `git push -u origin HEAD` (or push the current branch).
4. Do not wait for the user to say «ارفع» / «انشر».

Exceptions: do not push secrets, half-broken WIP the user asked to keep local, or destructive git ops (force push, hard reset) unless explicitly requested.
